   "text": "momcozy\nmomcozy\nmomcozy\nmomcozy\nmomcozy\nNo fever. Still congested.\nDo I take them in?\nFever is only half the story.\nHow long is too long.\nBREATHE EASY.\nWatch at home if:\nDON'T WAIT.\nCall the doctor if:\nA normal thermometer doesn't always mean\nall clear.\" But it's not a reason to panic either.\nWatch how they're breathing and acting-\nnot just the number.\nIt's 2 AM. You're staring at the crib. They sound\nawful. The thermometer says they're fine.\nYou're torn: \"Do I risk the waiting room germs,\nor am I waiting too long?11\nMost infant colds fade in 7-10 days\n(though congestion can linger).\nWatch For\nThe Safe Sign\nWatch For\nThe Red Flag\nSource: AAP Healthychildren 1healthyehildren.org / Children & Coldsl\nEating, sleeping, and smiling bet￿￿en sniffle&\nUnder 3 months old with any cold sign&\n4-6+ heavy wet diapers in 24 hour\nWorking hard: ribs sucking in, nostrils\nflaring, or breathing fast.\n#ILL\nDay7-10\nDay14\nOnset\nMost Common Colds Improve\nStill Not 8ette\nRelaxed and steady while asleep (no gasping).\nBlue-ish tint on lips or nail beds.\nCall the doctor ifr.\nSymptoms last1¢>14+ days without improving.\nThey get better, then suddenly get worse.\nHome Relief ChecklisL'\nNo wet diaper in 8+ hours, dry lips or crying\nwith no tears\nSaline drops\nCool-mist humidifier\nThe Bottom Line\nUpright snuggles {av4ake only)\nRefusing all feeds or very hard to wake up.\nTreat the baby, not the thermometer. You know them best.\nSwipe->\nSwipe->\nSouree: AAP HealthyChildrÈn / Penn MedicinÈ/ Sanford Health\nSouree: AAP He8￿hYchl1drÈn, Penn Medlcine. Sanford Health., AAP Safe Sleep Guidelines\nSwipe->\nSoure•: AAP HÈalthyChildren\"Children & Colds\"; Seattie ChildrÈn's'folds 1>12 Months\"\nSwipe->",
